ARM64 platform-register backport
================================

The imported GMP version remains 6.2.1.
Its ARM64 assembly uses x18 as a loop counter in ten routines.
Apple reserves this register for platform use.
The affected routines can fail intermittently in a Darwin host compiler.
Such a failure can read across the stack guard while the stack pointer remains near its normal location.
Increasing the stack size does not correct the register violation.

This tree backports the register changes from Torbjorn Granlund's GMP changeset f4ff6ff711ed:
https://gmplib.org/list-archives/gmp-commit/2020-November/003062.html
The mainline changeset is 5f32dbc41afc:
https://gmplib.org/list-archives/gmp-commit/2020-November/003063.html

The register allocation was also checked against the official GMP 6.3.0 release:
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gmp/gmp-6.3.0.tar.xz
Archive SHA256: a3c2b80201b89e68616f4ad30bc66aee4927c3ce50e33929ca819d5c43538898
Only the register changes are backported. Performance comments and other release changes are excluded.
The original authorship and GNU LGPL/GPL notices remain unchanged.

Apple ABI reference:
https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/writing-arm64-code-for-apple-platforms

Checks
------

From the EmberBSD source root:

    ruby ember/tests/gmp-darwin-registers.rb

On a Darwin ARM64 host, also pass freshly built GMP object files or its static archive.
The check inspects the actual object instructions with otool.
Run the upstream GMP make check suite in a separate native build directory.
Do not accept a compiler or target objects from the failing bootstrap build.
